util: bit counting without a library call on Mac OS X PowerPC

util_bitcount() is __builtin_popcount(), which on 32-bit PowerPC without
the popcntb instruction (every G4 and G5) is a call to libgcc's
__popcountsi2. glthread counts the user buffers of every draw that reads
client arrays (util_bitcount(user_buffer_mask), several times), and the
profile of The Sims 2 has __popcountsi2 at 1 % of the program's thread. A
parallel-sum count in registers is 12 instructions and no call.

--- a/src/util/bitscan.h	2026-10-23 13:19:32.536524956 -0300
+++ b/src/util/bitscan.h	2026-10-23 13:19:44.181237793 -0300
@@ -338,7 +338,16 @@
 static inline unsigned
 util_bitcount(unsigned n)
 {
-#if defined(HAVE___BUILTIN_POPCOUNT)
+#if defined(__APPLE__) && defined(__ppc__)
+   /* osx-gpu: the 32-bit PowerPC of Mac OS X (a G4 or G5) has no popcnt
+    * instruction, and __builtin_popcount is then a call to libgcc's
+    * __popcountsi2 (1 % of The Sims 2's thread: glthread counts the user
+    * buffers of every draw). Branch-free bit counting in registers. */
+   n = n - ((n >> 1) & 0x55555555u);
+   n = (n & 0x33333333u) + ((n >> 2) & 0x33333333u);
+   n = (n + (n >> 4)) & 0x0f0f0f0fu;
+   return (n * 0x01010101u) >> 24;
+#elif defined(HAVE___BUILTIN_POPCOUNT)
    return __builtin_popcount(n);
 #elif __OPENCL_VERSION__
    return popcount(n);
